{
  "summary": "Enables the `-Wunused-const-variable` compiler warning flag in CMake builds. To prevent warnings and errors across translation units where included headers do not use every variable, several constants in `src/logging.h` and `src/policy/fees/mempool_estimator.h` are marked `inline constexpr`.",
  "problem": "Header-declared `constexpr` variables without `inline` default to internal linkage, producing distinct instances in every translation unit that includes the header and triggering `-Wunused-const-variable` compilation failures when `-Werror` is active.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description demonstrates build failure: `error: ‘BCLog::RATELIMIT_MAX_BYTES’ defined but not used [-Werror=unused-const-variable=]`",
    "Author notes the work is split out of #36167 to enable broader unused warning flags"
  ],
